9	45	\N	\N	Hindi Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The official NCERT textbook prescribed by CBSE for Class 1 Hindi is Rimjhim - 1 (रिमझिम - १). It consists of 23 chapters filled with colorful illustrations, short poems, and simple stories designed to make language learning fun.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-09 10:50:09.15247	2026-06-09 10:50:09.15247
1	37	\N	\N	English Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	Comprehensive English syllabus designed for Class 1 students under the CBSE curriculum. This syllabus focuses on developing foundational language skills including reading, writing, vocabulary, grammar, listening, and communication. The content is structured progressively to support age-appropriate learning outcomes and academic development throughout the academic year.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-08 12:00:40.128049	2026-06-09 14:00:52.299817
20	350	\N	\N	Activity Based Learning Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The Activity Based Learning curriculum for Class 1 under the CBSE board shifts the focus from traditional textbook rote learning to an immersive, child-centric approach where doing leads to understanding. Designed specifically for the developmental needs of five- and six-year-olds, this syllabus integrates core subjects like Language, Mathematics, and Environmental Studies into hands-on experiences. By engaging the senses through play, exploration, and collaboration, the curriculum ensures that abstract concepts become concrete, meaningful, and enjoyable.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-12 17:49:05.584627	2026-06-17 11:49:02.028768
17	347	\N	\N	Dance Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The Dance curriculum for Class 1 under the CBSE board is structured as a form of creative expression and rhythmic movement rather than strict classical training. At this foundational stage, dance is used as a tool to help five- and six-year-olds develop spatial awareness, body coordination, and emotional expression. The syllabus focuses on making movement joyful, allowing children to explore the capabilities of their bodies while building confidence and a basic sense of rhythm.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-11 18:48:41.598723	2026-06-17 11:47:43.054112
21	42	\N	\N	English Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The CBSE Class 2 English curriculum focuses on transitioning young learners from basic word recognition to fluid reading, creative expression, and foundational grammar. The syllabus is structured around engaging stories, rhythmic poems, and interactive grammar exercises that build confidence in speaking, listening, reading, and writing.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-13 11:05:40.087264	2026-06-17 11:51:11.779255
15	345	\N	\N	Computer Education And Computer Awareness Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The Computer Education and Computer Awareness curriculum for Class 1 under the CBSE board serves as a gentle, foundational introduction to the digital world. At this early stage, the syllabus does not focus on complex coding or technical jargon. Instead, it aims to demystify technology for five- and six-year-olds, transforming computers from mysterious machines into familiar, helpful tools. The primary focus is on identifying basic hardware, understanding the core functions of a computer, and building foundational digital literacy through playful interaction.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-11 13:57:40.46891	2026-06-17 11:46:30.860965
44	70	\N	38	General Knowledge (GK) Syllabus For Class 3 CBSE Board	This engaging Class 3 General Knowledge course is designed to spark curiosity and expand young minds beyond the classroom. Aligned with the latest CBSE guidelines, it takes 3rd graders on a fun, interactive journey through the world around them. From the wonders of nature and the human body to Indian heritage, world geography, basic science, and everyday life skills, this course builds a strong foundation of awareness. Packed with vibrant themes, fun facts, and brain-teasing quizzes, it helps students develop critical thinking and a lifelong love for learning.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.098193	2026-06-19 13:59:48.098193
45	361	\N	33	Activity Based Learning Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Activity Based Learning approach for Class 2 under the CBSE board is an educational philosophy that shifts the focus from passive textbook memorization to active, student-centric exploration. Recognizing that seven- and eight-year-old children learn best by doing, this framework integrates hands-on experiences, play, and problem-solving into the core subjects of Mathematics, Language, and Environmental Studies. The ultimate goal is to move away from rote learning, making the classroom an interactive space where children construct knowledge through experiments, games, and physical manipulation of objects.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.099343	2026-06-19 13:59:48.099343
46	359	\N	31	Value Education And Moral Science Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Value Education and Moral Science curriculum for Class 2 is carefully structured to nurture the emotional, social, and ethical development of seven- to eight-year-old children. Rather than focusing on rigid academic concepts or rote learning, the syllabus aims to build character and instill core human values through relatable stories, real-life scenarios, and interactive classroom discussions. The primary objective is to help young learners differentiate between right and wrong, cultivate empathy, and develop a positive attitude toward their families, peers, and the environment.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.191385	2026-06-19 13:59:48.191385
47	358	\N	30	Dance Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The initial phase of the syllabus expands on basic motor control, helping children understand how different parts of their body can move independently and in unison. Students practice basic isolation techniques, learning to control their shoulders, waist, hands, and feet through rhythmic exercises. The syllabus introduces foundational concepts of balance and posture, teaching children how to maintain physical stability while shifting from high to medium and low levels in space. Exercises often incorporate free-flowing movements and fun tasks like freeze dancing to help children develop sudden muscle control, spatial awareness, and a sharp reflex to external musical cues.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.192254	2026-06-19 13:59:48.192254
48	362	\N	37	Environmental Studies (EVS) And The World Around Us Syllabus For Class 3 CBSE Board	Designed strictly in alignment with the latest CBSE guidelines, Environmental Studies (EVS) for Class 3 is an interactive journey that transforms young learners into curious explorers. This course bridges the gap between a child's immediate environment and the broader world, fostering a deep understanding of nature, society, and self.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.269815	2026-06-19 13:59:48.269815
8	46	\N	3	Mathematics Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The CBSE Class 1 Mathematics syllabus focuses on building foundational numerical literacy and logical thinking through engaging, hands-on concepts. Rather than complex calculations, the curriculum introduces young learners to basic arithmetic and spatial awareness, starting with Pre-Number concepts like comparing sizes (big/small), positions (top/bottom), and shapes. Students learn Numbers from 1 to 99, mastering counting, reading, writing, and understanding place value through tens and ones. This naturally progresses to introductory operational skills, specifically Single-Digit Addition and Subtraction using concrete objects and simple word problems. Additionally, the syllabus covers fundamental Geometry and Measurement, teaching kids to recognize basic 2D and 3D shapes (like circles, squares, and spheres) and estimate length and weight using non-standard units like handspans. To foster practical analytical skills, children are also introduced to Time (days of the week, reading simple clocks), Money (identifying Indian coins and currency notes), and basic Data Handling and Patterns, ensuring a well-rounded and practical introduction to everyday math.	2	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-08 18:30:23.41565	2026-06-17 11:18:50.386827
11	47	\N	\N	Environmental Studies (EVS) Syllabus for Class 1 CBSE Board	The CBSE Class 1 Environmental Studies (EVS) syllabus is a foundational curriculum designed to introduce young learners to their immediate surroundings. It focuses on developing observation skills, self-awareness, and environmental consciousness through simple, relatable themes.\n\nThe description of the core syllabus units includes:\n\nSelf and Family: Students learn to introduce themselves, identify their body parts and sense organs, and understand their family structure and the roles of family members.\n\nOur Basic Needs: This covers the essentials for life, including the types and sources of food, the uses of water, and the different clothes worn according to seasons.\n\nOur Neighborhood: An introduction to important places around them (like schools, hospitals, and parks) and the community helpers (such as doctors, teachers, and firefighters) who support daily life.\n\nThe Natural World: Children explore the world of plants and animals, learning to distinguish between domestic and wild animals, and identifying basic plant parts.\n\nWeather and Environment: A basic introduction to air, water usage, and how different weather conditions and seasons affect everyday life.\n\nGood Habits and Safety: Focuses on personal hygiene, good manners, and essential safety rules to follow at home, on the road, and at school.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-09 18:02:49.082752	2026-06-09 18:03:48.182534
10	37	\N	1	English Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	Comprehensive English syllabus designed for Class 1 students under the CBSE curriculum. This syllabus focuses on developing foundational language skills including reading, writing, vocabulary, grammar, listening, and communication. The content is structured progressively to support age-appropriate learning outcomes and academic development throughout the academic year.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-09 16:49:30.018909	2026-06-09 20:04:55.850904
12	50	\N	\N	General Knowledge (GK) Syllabus for Class 1 CBSE Board	The CBSE Class 1 General Knowledge syllabus is designed to build curiosity and foundational awareness in young learners aged 5 to 6 years. Instead of rigid academic testing, the curriculum focuses on interactive learning about the child's immediate world. It covers self-awareness by helping children learn about their family, school, and body parts, alongside an introduction to nature through common plants, fruits, and animals. It also instills early patriotism by teaching national symbols and major Indian festivals. Additionally, the syllabus introduces basic everyday concepts like weather, shapes, and modes of transport, while heavily emphasizing essential life skills such as good manners, personal hygiene, and road safety. Ultimately, the course uses stories, pictures, and quizzes to help children observe, understand, and safely navigate their environment.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-10 13:56:36.804581	2026-06-10 13:58:48.042638
13	53	\N	\N	Art and Craft Syllabus for Class 1 CBSE Board	CBSE Class 1 Art and Craft Syllabus Description\nThe Class 1 Art and Craft curriculum designed by the CBSE board focuses entirely on Expressive Arts, emphasizing joy, exploration, and the development of fundamental motor skills over artistic perfection. At this foundational stage, the syllabus gently introduces five- and six-year-olds to the world of colors, shapes, and textures through hands-on activities that boost hand-eye coordination and spatial awareness.\n\nDrawing and Coloring Foundations\nThe journey begins with the building blocks of visual art, where children learn to identify and replicate basic lines and shapes. Students practice drawing straight, curved, and zig-zag lines, which gradually transition into forming geometric shapes like circles, squares, triangles, and rectangles. The curriculum guides them to look at the world around them and recognize these shapes in everyday objects. Activities include connecting dots to form pictures and practicing the control needed to color neatly within boundary lines using thick crayons or oil pastels. Typical drawing subjects include simple, recognizable figures such as a bright sun, a basic house, colorful balloons, or an umbrella.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-10 17:11:46.659024	2026-06-10 17:11:46.659024
14	344	\N	\N	Health and Physical Education Syllabus for Class 1 CBSE Board	The Health and Physical Education curriculum for Class 1 under the CBSE board is designed to foster a positive attitude toward physical fitness, hygiene, and overall well-being from a young age. Instead of intense sports training or complex theoretical concepts, the syllabus focuses on joyful movement, spatial awareness, basic coordination, and foundational healthy habits. The primary goal is to help five- and six-year-olds develop control over their bodies while learning how to keep themselves clean, safe, and active.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-11 10:57:11.746992	2026-06-11 10:57:11.746992
18	348	\N	\N	Value Education And Moral Science Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The Value Education and Moral Science curriculum for Class 1 under the CBSE board focuses on nurturing the hearts and minds of young children, helping them build a strong moral foundation at the very beginning of their formal schooling. Rather than teaching complex ethical philosophies, the syllabus introduces core human values through relatable situations, engaging stories, and everyday interactions. The primary objective is to instill positive behavioral traits, emotional intelligence, and a sense of responsibility toward oneself, the family, the community, and the environment.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-12 12:42:31.204592	2026-06-17 11:48:00.47109
19	349	\N	\N	Spoken English Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The Spoken English curriculum for Class 1 under the CBSE board aims to build a strong foundation for oral communication, listening comprehension, and vocal confidence. Recognizing that five- and six-year-olds are at a critical stage for language acquisition, the syllabus prioritizes interactive, high-energy verbal engagement over formal written grammar rules. The primary objective is to eliminate the fear of speaking in a second language and to help children express their thoughts, needs, and feelings clearly and confidently in everyday situations.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-12 15:59:44.498656	2026-06-17 11:48:42.963117
26	351	\N	\N	Computer Education And Computer Awareness Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Computer Education curriculum for Class 2 under the CBSE board is designed to transition young learners from basic recognition to a more operational understanding of technology. Building upon what they observed in early childhood, the syllabus aims to make children comfortable with digital environments while emphasizing safe, responsible handling of machines. The primary focus is on identifying core hardware components, understanding how computers assist humans in daily life, and developing foundational input skills like typing and clicking.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-15 17:17:15.224705	2026-06-17 11:52:19.971154
25	60	\N	\N	General Knowledge (GK) Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The General Knowledge curriculum for Class 2 under the CBSE board is designed to broaden a child’s horizon beyond their standard textbooks. At this early developmental stage, the syllabus focuses on sparking curiosity, enhancing observation skills, and building a strong foundational awareness of the immediate environment, the country, and the wider world. The content is kept interactive, relatable, and visually engaging to ensure that seven- and eight-year-olds can easily absorb information about nature, science, language, and daily life.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-15 15:12:56.741395	2026-06-17 11:52:40.122796
24	58	\N	\N	Environmental Studies (EVS) Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Environmental Studies curriculum for Class 2 under the CBSE board is designed to expand a child's awareness beyond themselves to the immediate world around them. At this stage, the syllabus transitions from basic self-awareness to exploring relationships, nature, community, and the environment. The focus is on nurturing curiosity, observation skills, and a sense of responsibility toward nature and society through relatable, everyday themes.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-15 12:24:50.488716	2026-06-17 11:53:08.918063
22	56	\N	\N	Hindi Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Class 2 Hindi curriculum designed by the CBSE board aims to build upon the foundational language skills acquired in the previous year, transitioning students from basic alphabet recognition to meaningful communication. The syllabus focuses on developing the four core language pillars: listening, speaking, reading, and writing. At this level, the curriculum uses engaging stories, lyrical poems, and simple grammar concepts to help seven-year-olds express their thoughts confidently, read fluently, and appreciate the beauty of the Hindi language in their daily lives.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-13 13:39:16.397931	2026-06-17 11:53:55.050588
43	67	\N	36	Mathematics Syllabus For Class 3 CBSE Board	In Class 3, Mathematics transitions from basic counting into exciting real-world problem-solving! Following the latest CBSE and NCERT guidelines, this course is designed to build a strong foundational understanding of numbers, shapes, and measurements through fun, relatable, and interactive concepts.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.059496	2026-06-19 13:59:48.059496
3	46	\N	\N	Mathematics Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The CBSE Class 1 Mathematics syllabus focuses on building foundational numerical literacy and logical thinking through engaging, hands-on concepts. Rather than complex calculations, the curriculum introduces young learners to basic arithmetic and spatial awareness, starting with Pre-Number concepts like comparing sizes (big/small), positions (top/bottom), and shapes. Students learn Numbers from 1 to 99, mastering counting, reading, writing, and understanding place value through tens and ones. This naturally progresses to introductory operational skills, specifically Single-Digit Addition and Subtraction using concrete objects and simple word problems. Additionally, the syllabus covers fundamental Geometry and Measurement, teaching kids to recognize basic 2D and 3D shapes (like circles, squares, and spheres) and estimate length and weight using non-standard units like handspans. To foster practical analytical skills, children are also introduced to Time (days of the week, reading simple clocks), Money (identifying Indian coins and currency notes), and basic Data Handling and Patterns, ensuring a well-rounded and practical introduction to everyday math.	2	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-08 17:49:38.265543	2026-06-17 10:39:33.114792
16	346	\N	\N	Music Syllabus For Class 1 CBSE Board	The Music curriculum for Class 1 under the CBSE board is designed to be a joyful, immersive introduction to the world of sound, rhythm, and vocal expression. At this foundational stage, the syllabus does not focus on rigorous classical training or complex music theory. Instead, it aims to develop a child's auditory discrimination, voice modulation, sense of rhythm, and emotional expression through playful, group-oriented musical activities. The primary goal is to make children comfortable with their own voices and to foster a lifelong love for music.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-11 17:11:39.887291	2026-06-17 11:47:18.552
27	355	\N	\N	Art and Craft And Drawing Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Art, Craft, and Drawing curriculum for Class 2 under the CBSE board builds upon the basic foundations laid in the previous year, guiding seven-year-olds toward a deeper exploration of creative expression and structural design. At this level, the syllabus moves beyond simple random scribbling to encourage more deliberate compositions, refined fine motor coordination, and an understanding of spatial relationships. The curriculum blends drawing, coloring, craftwork, and innovative print techniques to make art a deeply engaging, sensory, and joyful learning experience.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-15 18:40:13.46274	2026-06-17 11:51:30.578491
28	356	\N	\N	Health and Physical Education (HPE) Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Health and Physical Education curriculum for Class 2 under the CBSE board builds smoothly upon the foundational movements learned in the previous year. For seven-year-olds, the focus shifts slightly from simple independent movements to more deliberate physical control, rhythmic coordination, and a deeper understanding of personal health and community hygiene. The curriculum aims to make physical activity a natural, joyful part of daily life while instilling lifelong habits of wellness, safety, and teamwork.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-16 13:28:08.785852	2026-06-17 11:51:43.802347
29	357	\N	\N	Music Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Music curriculum for Class 2 under the CBSE board is structured around joyful exploration, vocal discovery, and sensory interaction with sounds. Following the National Curriculum Framework for the Foundational Stage, the syllabus emphasizes the pure enjoyment of making music rather than strict performance outcomes. At the age of seven and eight, children are encouraged to build a strong connection with rhythm, match pitch naturally, and use their voices and bodies as tools for creative expression.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-17 10:34:27.687791	2026-06-17 11:51:55.234732
40	66	\N	35	Hindi Syllabus For Class 3 CBSE Board	Step into the vibrant world of Hindi language and literature! Designed strictly according to the CBSE curriculum, this course guides Class 3 students through engaging stories, playful poems, and essential grammar. Students will transition from basic word formation to reading with comprehension, expressing original thoughts, and writing creatively. Through beautifully illustrated chapters, children will expand their vocabulary, master fundamental grammar rules, and build a lasting love for the language.	1	f	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:47.244338	2026-06-19 13:59:47.244338
23	40	\N	\N	Mathematics Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Class 2 Mathematics curriculum under the CBSE board is designed to transition young learners from basic counting to a deeper understanding of mathematical concepts and logical thinking. At this stage, the syllabus moves beyond simple memorization, focusing instead on building a strong foundation in number sense, basic arithmetic operations, spatial awareness, and real-world application. The primary objective is to make mathematics relatable, helping seven- and eight-year-olds see how numbers and shapes function in their everyday environments.\nThe syllabus significantly expands the child’s numerical world by introducing three-digit numbers. Students learn to read, write, and count numbers up to one thousand, understanding the sequence and order of these values. A critical milestone in this segment is the introduction of place value, where children learn to break down a number into hundreds, tens, and ones. This conceptual understanding helps them confidently compare numbers using terms like greater than, less than, and equal to. Additionally, children are introduced to foundational number patterns, including skip counting by twos, fives, and tens, as well as distinguishing between even and odd numbers.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-15 11:01:05.575755	2026-06-17 11:53:31.335399
30	358	\N	\N	Dance Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The initial phase of the syllabus expands on basic motor control, helping children understand how different parts of their body can move independently and in unison. Students practice basic isolation techniques, learning to control their shoulders, waist, hands, and feet through rhythmic exercises. The syllabus introduces foundational concepts of balance and posture, teaching children how to maintain physical stability while shifting from high to medium and low levels in space. Exercises often incorporate free-flowing movements and fun tasks like freeze dancing to help children develop sudden muscle control, spatial awareness, and a sharp reflex to external musical cues.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-17 11:59:38.327362	2026-06-17 12:00:37.299542
31	359	\N	\N	Value Education And Moral Science Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Value Education and Moral Science curriculum for Class 2 is carefully structured to nurture the emotional, social, and ethical development of seven- to eight-year-old children. Rather than focusing on rigid academic concepts or rote learning, the syllabus aims to build character and instill core human values through relatable stories, real-life scenarios, and interactive classroom discussions. The primary objective is to help young learners differentiate between right and wrong, cultivate empathy, and develop a positive attitude toward their families, peers, and the environment.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-17 13:11:58.176353	2026-06-17 13:12:16.165155
32	360	\N	\N	Spoken English Syllabus For Class 2 CBSE Board	The Spoken English curriculum for Class 2 under the CBSE guidelines is built to transform passive language knowledge into active, confident communication. At this developmental stage, seven- and eight-year-olds already have a foundational vocabulary, so the syllabus shifts focus toward sentence structure, correct pronunciation, and social communication. The entire framework is designed to be highly interactive, eliminating formal grammar lectures in favor of immersive, speech-heavy activities that remove the fear of speaking in a second language.	1	t	t	\N	\N	2026-06-17 15:31:33.059174	2026-06-17 15:31:50.076533
