73	9	69	Sarvanaam (सर्वनाम)	Sarvanaam (सर्वनाम) introduces young learners to the foundational concept of Pronouns. In simple, child-friendly language, the chapter is often titled "Naam ki Jagah" (In place of names). It teaches children that instead of repeating a person's, animal's, or object's name (Sangya / Noun) over and over again in a conversation or paragraph, we can use shorter words. For example, instead of saying "Rahul is a good boy. Rahul goes to school," we say "Rahul is a good boy. He goes to school." Class 1 students are introduced to basic everyday pronouns like:  मैं (I)  तुम (You)  वह (He/She/It)  यह (This)  हम (We)  वे (They)	chapter	4	4	By the end of this chapter, young students will successfully recognize that words used in place of naming words are called Sarvanaam. They will develop the ability to construct clearer, more natural-sounding sentences by avoiding unnecessary repetition of names. Practically, outcomes include the child's ability to confidently choose the correct pronoun to fill in blanks (such as pairing मैं with हूँ or हम with हैं) and apply these pronouns accurately in both their spoken language and early Hindi writing skills.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-09 13:47:38.626038	2026-06-09 13:47:38.626038
