291	17	289	The Butterfly Glide	The Butterfly Glide is a graceful imitative movement where children mimic the gentle, fluttering flight of a butterfly. In this activity, children extend their arms out like wings and move them up and down in soft, rhythmic waves while moving around the room on their tiptoes. Through this playful dance, they use creative facial expressions and light body movements to bring the story of a happy, gliding butterfly to life, blending basic dance steps with imaginative storytelling (Abhinaya).	chapter	1	4	Participating in The Butterfly Glide helps young children develop emotional expression, imagination, and basic rhythm. By translating the concept of a butterfly into movement, children learn the fundamentals of Abhinaya (expression), discovering how to communicate feelings and narratives without words. Physically, the activity improves gross motor skills, balance, and body flexibility, while fostering a sense of rhythm and spatial awareness as they glide gracefully through the performance area.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-12 11:46:59.102033	2026-06-12 11:46:59.102033
