270	16	269	Melodic Instruments	Melodic instruments are musical instruments that can play a sequence of different notes to create a beautiful, singing tune or melody, rather than just a rhythmic beat. In Class 1, children are introduced to simple and recognizable melodic instruments like the flute (bansuri), the harmonium, and the violin or sitar. Through fun, interactive listening games and colorful visuals, young learners discover how these instruments use air, keys, or strings to produce high and low sounds. The focus is on helping children distinctively recognize the unique, sweet sound (timbre) that each instrument makes, sparking their natural curiosity about the world of melody.	chapter	7	4	By the end of this chapter, young learners will be able to effortlessly identify common melodic instruments by sight and distinguish their unique sounds from one another. Students will develop enhanced auditory listening skills, allowing them to notice the difference between a wind instrument like the flute and a stringed instrument like the sitar. Additionally, this unit nurtures an early appreciation for both Indian classical and Western music, building a foundational vocabulary for self-expression and laying a joyful groundwork for their own future musical journeys.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-11 18:02:47.989104	2026-06-11 18:02:47.989104
