389	21	384	Prepositions (Position Words)	Prepositions introduces young learners to the concept of "position words" in a highly visual, interactive, and oral-focused manner. Instead of focusing on complex grammatical definitions, the chapter uses everyday objects and relatable scenarios to show how words like in, on, under, near, behind, and between tell us where a person, animal, or object is located. Through fun spoken activities, picture matching, and storytelling, students learn to connect objects to their spatial positions. The content is specifically designed to build confidence in spoken English, encouraging children to move from single-word answers to forming simple, complete sentences when describing their surroundings.	chapter	15	4	Identify Position Words: Recognize and point out basic prepositions ($in$, $on$, $under$, $behind$, $near$, $between$) in spoken sentences and illustrated stories.Describe Spatial Relationships: Confidently describe the location of objects around them in real-time (e.g., "The book is on the table," "The cat is under the chair").Respond to Verbal Prompts: Listen to oral instructions involving positions and react accurately, such as placing a pencil inside a box or standing next to a peer.Enhance Spoken Sentence Structure: Progress from using fragmented phrases to constructing grammatically correct, simple sentences when explaining where things are.Apply Concepts in Daily Conversation: Naturally integrate position words into their daily communication, improving their overall fluency, clarity, and foundational English composition skills.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-13 12:58:24.577249	2026-06-13 12:58:24.577249
