406	22	\N	Jeevan-Jagat (जीवन-जगत - The World Around Us)	The unit Jeevan-Jagat (The World Around Us) acts as a gentle, literary window to nature for second-grade students, featuring a delightful mix of stories, poems, and interactive picture conversations. Through chapters like Taalaab (The Pond), Beej (The Seed), Kisaan (The Farmer), Mooli (The Radish), and Barsat aur Mendhak (The Rain and the Frog), the unit takes children on a journey through rural and natural landscapes. It creatively illustrates environmental processes—such as how a tiny seed transitions into a green plant, the essential relationship between a farmer and agriculture, and how seasonal cycles bring life to ecosystems like ponds and rainy fields. By centering the narratives around relatable elements like water bodies, plants, animals, and weather changes, the text builds a vibrant, eco-conscious vocabulary and encourages students to closely observe and appreciate the flora and fauna surrounding them.	unit	2	4	Upon completing this unit, young learners transition from passive observers to curious and empathetic appreciators of their natural environment. Beyond strengthening core language competencies—such as phonological awareness, expanded Hindi vocabulary for natural elements, and sentence formation—students develop a foundational sense of ecological responsibility. They learn to view trees, water bodies, and animals not just as resources, but as cohabitants of a colorful world, grasping basic concepts of life cycles and the crucial role humans play in sustaining agriculture. Ultimately, the pedagogical outcome blends language acquisition with moral growth, cultivating an early sense of environmental mindfulness and active empathy toward all living beings.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-13 16:03:20.950276	2026-06-13 16:03:34.618714
