432	22	430	Maatra Abhyas (मात्रा अभ्यास)	In the Class 2 Hindi Grammar curriculum, "Maatra Abhyas" serves as a foundational chapter designed to transition students from reading isolated letters to constructing and understanding full words and sentences. While students are introduced to vowels (स्वर) and consonants (व्यंजन) in Class 1, this chapter deeply explores how vowels change their forms into symbols called Maatras when they combine with consonants.The chapter systematically guides students through each vowel sign—from the inherent '$a$' sound (अ) which has no symbol, to the complex sounds like '$au$' (औ), as well as the nasal sounds (Anusvaar and Anunasik). Through engaging exercises, colorful illustrations, and word-formation drills, students learn the precise placement of these symbols—whether they go above, below, before, or after a consonant. It addresses common pain points for young learners, such as distinguishing between short and long vowel sounds (like '$i$' $\\text{\\bf\\u{i}}$ vs '$ee$' $\\text{\\bf\\bar{e}}$ in 'इ' and 'ई', or '$u$' vs '$oo$' in 'उ' and 'ऊ'), which is essential for accurate spelling and pronunciation.	chapter	27	4	Identify and Differentiate Symbols: Recognize all Hindi vowel signs (Maatras) and accurately identify which symbol belongs to which vowel.Master Correct Placement: Understand the structural rules of Hindi script, knowing exactly where to place a Maatra relative to a consonant (e.g., 'ि' goes before, 'ी' goes after, 'ु' goes below, and 'े' goes above).Enhance Pronunciation and Phonics: Pronounce words accurately by understanding the phonetic difference between short vowels (ह्रस्व स्वर) and long vowels (दीर्घ स्वर), drastically reducing common speech hesitations.Build Vocabulary and Spelling Accuracy: Form new, meaningful words independently and minimize spelling errors ($वर्तनी$) by correctly applying the appropriate vowel signs.Develop Reading and Writing Fluency: Read simple sentences smoothly and express their thoughts 