440	22	430	Kriya (क्रिया - Verbs)	In the Class 2 Hindi Grammar syllabus, the chapter "Kriya" introduces young learners to the fundamental concept of action words. At this primary level, the topic is taught using simple, relatable language and vibrant visual examples.\n\nThe chapter explains that Kriya refers to words that tell us about an action being done or happening naturally. Children learn to identify everyday actions—such as khana (eating), peena (drinking), rona (crying), khelna (playing), and padhna (reading). The lessons are designed to help students notice that no sentence in Hindi is complete without an action word. The chapter also gently introduces the idea that some actions are performed by us intentionally (like writing a letter), while others happen on their own in nature (like the sun rising or rain falling).	chapter	35	4	Identify Action Words: Recognize and point out Kriya (verb) words in simple sentences and daily conversations.\n\nUnderstand Sentence Structure: Comprehend that a sentence requires an action word to convey a complete meaning.\n\nDifferentiate Action Types: Distinguish between actions done by human effort and actions that happen naturally in the environment.\n\nEnhance Vocabulary: Expand their Hindi vocabulary with a wide range of common verbs used in daily routines.\n\nApply Correct Usage: Use appropriate verb forms in speaking and writing, ensuring proper sentence construction based on the subject.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-13 19:01:37.943939	2026-06-13 19:01:37.943939
