826	40	801	किसान की होशियारी (Kisaan Ki Hoshiyaari)	The story "किसान की होशियारी" is a classic folktale about a clever farmer and a foolish bear (or sometimes a tiger or demon, depending on regional variations in folk literature) who wants to take over the farmer's land. Instead of panicking or fighting, the wise farmer uses his quick wit and presence of mind to outsmart the wild animal. He strikes a deal with the bear to divide the harvest, cleverly tricking the bear multiple times by altering what crops he grows. When the bear demands the top half of the crop, the farmer grows potatoes (getting the nutritious roots for himself). When the frustrated bear switches his demand to the roots for the next harvest, the farmer smartly grows wheat or sugarcane, leaving the bear with useless roots once again. Through his tactical intelligence, the farmer saves his livelihood and protects his farm without resorting to violence.	chapter	14	4	The primary learning outcome of this chapter is to teach young students the value of presence of mind, critical thinking, and situational awareness when facing difficult challenges. Falling perfectly under the unit theme of Awareness and Identity, the story helps children recognize that physical strength can easily be overcome by intelligence and calm reasoning. Students learn to think creatively to solve problems instead of getting scared in tough situations. Additionally, on a practical level, the chapter enhances the students' vocabulary regarding farming, crops, and nature, while building a strong moral foundation that wit and patience are a person's greatest strengths.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:47.244338	2026-06-19 13:59:47.244338
