847	42	\N	Hindi Grammar Syllabus (व्याकरण)	The Class 2 Hindi Grammar curriculum is designed to transition young learners from basic letter recognition to structured sentence formation and meaningful communication. It introduces foundational linguistic concepts through relatable examples, engaging stories, and simple exercises.\n\nStudents explore the core building blocks of the language, starting with letters and words, and moving into essential parts of speech and basic vocabulary expansion. The primary focus is on making children aware of the rules of the language naturally, without overloading them with complex definitions.	section	6	4	भाषा और व्याकरण (Language & Grammar): Understanding what language is and its oral/written forms.\n\nवर्ण और वर्णमाला (Letters & Alphabet): Reintroducing vowels (स्वर), consonants (व्यंजन), and joint letters (संयुक्त व्यंजन).\n\nमात्राएँ (Vowel Signs): Correct application of vowel symbols on consonants.\n\nशब्द और वाक्य (Words & Sentences): How letters combine to form words, and words combine to make meaningful sentences.\n\nसंज्ञा (Noun): Identifying names of people, places, animals, and things (नाम वाले शब्द).\n\nलिंग (Gender): Distinguishing between masculine (पुल्लिंग) and feminine (स्त्रीलिंग) words (जैसे: लड़का-लड़की, राजा-रानी).\n\nवचन (Number): Understanding singular and plural concepts (एक-अनेक, जैसे: लड़का-लड़के).\n\nसर्वनाम (Pronoun): Words used in place of nouns (नाम की जगह आने वाले शब्द, जैसे: मैं, तुम, वह).\n\nविशेषण (Adjective): Describing words (विशेषता बताने वाले शब्द, जैसे: बड़ा, सुंदर, चार).\n\nक्रिया (Verb): Action words (काम वाले शब्द, जैसे: पढ़ना, खेलना, खाना).\n\nसामान्य शब्द (Basic Vocabulary): Introduction to synonyms (पर्यायवाची), antonyms (विलोम शब्द), and days of the week/months.\n\nरचनात्मक लेखन (Creative Writing): Short paragraph writing (अनुच्छेद लेखन) and picture description (चित्र वर्णन).	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.03397	2026-06-19 13:59:48.03397
