927	45	897	The Bundles of Joy (Place Value - Tens & Ones)	"The Bundles of Joy" introduces second-grade students to the foundational concept of place value through an engaging, hands-on Activity-Based Learning (ABL) approach. Instead of relying on abstract rules, the chapter uses concrete objects like sticks, straws, or beads that children can physically group into "bundles of ten" alongside loose "ones." By counting and creating these bundles, young learners visually and tactilely understand how two-digit numbers are constructed. This playful, interactive method bridges the gap between simple counting and mathematical notation, transforming a crucial math concept into an enjoyable game of organizing and discovering patterns.	chapter	6	4	By the end of this chapter, students will be able to confidently identify, represent, and manipulate two-digit numbers by breaking them down into their respective tens and ones places. They will develop the ability to group individual objects into sets of ten, establishing a strong conceptual understanding that a "bundle" represents a single unit of ten. Furthermore, students will apply this knowledge to read, write, and compare numbers up to 99, expressing them accurately in both expanded form and standard notation. Ultimately, this foundational mastery of place value will enhance their mental math skills and seamlessly prepare them for more advanced operations like addition and subtraction with regrouping.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-19 13:59:48.099343	2026-06-19 13:59:48.099343
