1044	38	1043	Traffic Rules and Road Safety Signage	This chapter introduces young learners to the foundational concepts of road safety and the essential rules of the road. It covers basic yet critical habits, such as using the zebra crossing to walk across the street, walking strictly on the footpath, and understanding the classic "Stop, Look, and Listen" rule before stepping off a curb. Students are introduced to the meaning of standard traffic lights (Red means Stop, Yellow means Wait/Get Ready, and Green means Go) as well as common road signs like the School Ahead, No Horn, and Pedestrian Crossing signs. Through simple visuals and relatable scenarios, the lesson teaches children that roads are shared public spaces that require caution, patience, and alertness.	chapter	28	4	After completing this chapter, students will be able to recognize and explain basic traffic signals and road signs, moving from passive passengers to active, safety-conscious pedestrians. They will develop the life skill of situational awareness, understanding exactly how and where to cross a street safely to prevent accidents. Most importantly, the lesson instills a sense of personal responsibility and respect for civic rules from an early age, ensuring that children value not only their own safety but also the safety of others on the road.	{}	t	\N	\N	2026-06-20 05:43:02.196017	2026-06-20 05:43:02.196017
